  "rationale": "Focused CRISPR knockout screen in KRAS-mutant A549-Cas9 cells with a minipool of 483 sgRNAs targeting 80 lung-cancer tumour-suppressor genes plus 12 positive-control essential genes and 26 negative 'safe' sgRNAs. Cells carrying the library were given either a non-targeting guide (sgNeg) or a guide against UHRF1 (sgUHRF1), then passaged; DNA was collected at T0 (split) and T1 (18 days). The paper (Supplementary Data 10) reports a depletion z-score for each gene separately in the sgNeg and the sgUHRF1 background, to find tumour-suppressor knockouts whose fitness effect depends on UHRF1. Each background is reproduced as its own T1-vs-T0 contrast with two replicates per timepoint (2 residual df). The A549TSGlibT0 plasmid library column is not part of either contrast. 'safe' sgRNAs are the negative controls.",
